			<div class="content" id="post-content-4811513">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Love, Drama/Emotional, Action, Mystery (Mild)</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>This is a longer article.</strong></li>
<li>Standard containment procedures and description, nothing too special.</li>
<li>Standard addendums where D-Class were sent in.</li>
<li>The only weird features of this article is that the last few addendums are accessible by Level 4 Personnel with the rest of the document being accessible by Level 2 personnel.</li>
<li>The actual anomaly is explained in the <span style="text-decoration: underline;">Elevator Pitch</span> while the main story is told in the <span style="text-decoration: underline;">Central Narrative and the Hook/Attention Grabber</span>.</li>
<li>CANON DISCLAIMER: This anomaly is a bit contradicting to Corbenic, but my excuse to make this dimension different is that it is only experienced through individuals who don’t follow a religion. Other plot holes that intertwine with Corbenic I would like to use the “<em>there is no canon</em>“ statement of the wiki.</li>
</ul>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Tab&nbsp;For&nbsp;Space</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">My&nbsp;Concept/Idea</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong><br />
The anomaly is located within Bryce Canyon National Park, where a dimension (at a certain time of night) anomalously takes the place of the park. The dimension is a series of caves and caverns, containing both a collection of “demons” and individuals who have died and do not profess to any religion or cult. The demons essentially judge living and dead individuals, forcefully taking individuals to certain caverns based on their life choices. Some are tortured, others peacefully relax, while non-affected people can leave the dimension.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
The first addendums show D-Class exploration logs, following former Research Head “Harry” and his professional experimentation. After a D-Class was able to return with her daughter however, research is strangely ramped up by Harry, as he becomes more and more unprofessional. After some redacted events, Harry is replaced with a new research head. The file eventually allows the reader to view an un-redacted version of the final addendums, being Level 4 Files.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong><br />
The redacted event is described, as Harry and an MTF travel through the dimension. The MTF is picked off as the soldiers are taken to different caverns by the demons. Some are seen relaxing while other are tortured, but Harry is the last one remaining in the group. Eventually he finds a placid forest where he finds a woman, both happily embracing. They attempt to leave the cavern, but the demons block the woman from leaving. After a short discussion, they kiss and Harry leaves the dimension.</p>
<p>An interview is conducted, with Harry revealing his motives. His wife was a researcher who died in a containment breach, and ever since then he wanted to find a way to resurrect her. When he saw the dimension, he wanted to find out if people can be functionally resurrected, killing an unnecessary amount of D-Class for his studies. He decided to go, successfully finding his wife. After being barred however, he realized that while he can leave, she was always destined to die in that event, with no way of reversing it.</p>
<p>For his actions, he was reprimanded and demoted to a Level 2 Clearance, later found dead in his offices from suicide.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong><br />
An exploration log shows him and his wife peacefully in the forest, a sort of happy ending.</p>
</div>
</div>
