			<div class="content" id="post-content-4811874">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>After an anomalous event, the UIU begin a file after finding an anomalous harp.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm assuming the harp is in some way related to the event?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>find that the GOC, Serpent’s Hand (SH), and Chaos Insurgency (CI) are starting a war with hundreds of civilian casualties.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why are they starting a war with a lot of civilian casualties? Why are the TMI/Foundation not paying enough attention to notice this already? How does this war actually like, tie into the narrative here?</p>
<p>Like the war seems kinda important to the SCP but also kinda&#8230;background-y? It's weird.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the GOC Leader (who is anomalous) loved Orpheus</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The idea of the GOC having like, one leader who can just, unilaterally decide to do things feels kinda jarring? Like, arguably D.C. al Fine is the leader but she has to answer to the UN and a secret council of 108 so like&#8230;it feels weird that she can just do all this for personal reasons without being fired?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>After finding the UIU helping Orpheus, all 4 of them go to Three Portlands to find Eurydice, with Three Portlands being in civil unrest as a war for civil rights occurs.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&#8230;why do the UIU team up here?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>They all allied after realizing that killing an O5 member would be a powerful enough message.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't understand why they allied here? The GOC have very different aims to the SH/CI here; and it's not even clear why the CI/SH are aligned cos they also have generally different aims.</p>
<hr />
<p>I think, at the end of the day, my issue with this is that there's a lot of moving parts and stuff going on here and it feels&#8230;bloated? Like, you have 6 different GoIs<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-331436-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-331436-1')">1</a></sup> involved in this story and big plot twists relating to like two different leaders of the GoIs and there's this whole thing about them being greek folk but it doesn't particularly seem to matter really beyond the reference to the classical myth. It's hard to put my finger on what this feels like it's missing exactly but I think it's a sense of&#8230;coherence? I don't really follow why these events are occurring or what's motivating folk here; so it just feels very arbitrary in a way that doesn't really jive with me.</p>
<p>This being a SCP article feels like a huge mistake too; like, it feels like you could tell a much tighter story if you didn't have to worry about e.g. clinical tone or how the Foundation got certain logs, and instead could just&#8230;prose it up, y'know? Show the story unfolding from the PoV of the various GoIs involved, really let us get into the head of Orpheus and stuff and understand why they're so driven and all that.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
