				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jacob-conwell" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1372582); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1372582&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607070128" alt="Jacob Conwell" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1372582)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jacob-conwell" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1372582); return false;" >Jacob Conwell</a></span> <span class="odate time_1604792750 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">07 Nov 2020 23:45</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4813393">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>After hundreds of people arrive in Corbenic, the Three Moons Initiative begin a joint operation with the Foundation to find out what is happening.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Can the TMI not just ask the people who arrived in Corbenic what happened?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>They join the UIU as they survey the damage of Three Portlands and find the bodies of O5 members in anomalously destroyed sites.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm confused, is this implying that the SCPF has sites in Three Portlands? Obviously &quot;no canons&quot; applies, but that goes super counter to a huge amount of the established lore of 3Ports, namely the Foundation is super not welcome there. If not, then how did the Foundation not notice ENTIRE SITES being destroyed sooner?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>They see a battle take place before the Gate Guardian crashes down and stops the battle.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The hell is the Gate Guardian doing there? Its been a while, but last I checked the Gate Guardian is very much guarding a single location.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The SH begins a civil rights movement for reality benders in Three Portlands</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;No canons&quot; rules applying again, but 3Ports is generally viewed as the kind of place where reality benders would already be viewed as people. That kind of civil rights movement wouldn't really be needed there. At all.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Three Portlands undergoes a civil war as Activist fight against Foundation sympathizers, who believe that reality benders are too powerful to be treated normally.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Foundation sympathizers would generally be in such a low minority in Three Portlands that this would be a very small and heavily one-sided conflict.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This war causes hundreds of people to arrive at Corbenic.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why would this stand out compared to any other reason people die and arrive on Corbenic for any other mundane reason on a given day?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The SH and CI realize that to win this war, they must destroy the Foundation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Last I checked, both the SH and the CI kind of have the destruction of the Foundation as an end goal as a default. This really doesn't seem like a thing they would just now, after starting a civil war, would realize.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The SH, CI, and GOC begin hunting the O5 Council, killing Eurydice first and injuring Orpheus (a reality bender with his anomalous harp).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How do they know where the O5 council is?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>convincing the O5 Council (besides O5-1 because he was assigned to the investigation) to help him.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why would the O5 members, with the ENTIRE SCP FOUNDATION at their disposal try to go this mission themselves instead of delegating it to what I'm sure are a multitude of much, much better trained MTFs?</p>
<hr />
<p>All in all, my overall impression is that you throw a lot of GoIs into this, but don't really quite use them effectively, and often come across as if you only have a cursory understanding of what it is that makes reading about each of them fun to explore. I'd argue parring this down to just focus on the SH would likely be most in tune for what you are going for, since it would seem to me that CI and GOC involvement just adds bloat and doesn't really add that much to the story.</p>
<p>A retelling of the Orpheus myth in the SCP Foundation universe certainly could fly with the correct execution. But as of the time of writing, I don't think this would be it.</p>
<p>Best of luck.</p>
</div>
</div>
