<p><strong>Thank you very much for the critique.</strong></p>
<p>I was going to make some changes to the concept before you responded, but some of the points you had were pretty solid. Here are my changes:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">^&nbsp;Changes</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">&gt;&nbsp;List&nbsp;of&nbsp;Changes</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>Was initially going to remove the “wish granter” as I thought it was too reflective of the original story. After your response, I decided that the cognitohazards are not as important as I thought and opted for the demons instead. This was because I thought why would a God of The Underworld spend all his time judging the living and the dead, why not have demons do the work for you. So in conclusion, <span style="text-decoration: underline;">I removed the cognitohazards and the wish granter to highlight the demons</span>.</li>
<li>The demons (originally the cognitohazards) are kind of necessary as they are like the “judge, jury, and executioner” of this version of the underworld. This also is another reason why I removed the wish granter since the demons are kind of doing the job for them. So essentially, <span style="text-decoration: underline;">the demons usually do the job of Hades</span>.</li>
<li>Now with modifying the concept of the Underworld, it would make the writing process easier but I just wanted to focus on the story and the main items necessary for the story. That was the main reason why I made an underworld from scratch. Not to mention, I do want to point out that this version of the underworld is reserved “for people who don’t profess to a religion,” so it’s not a fully developed underworld. So basically, <span style="text-decoration: underline;">the Underworld I made is a small branch of something that can be expanded on</span>.</li>
<li>I decided to make the location of the anomaly in Bryce Canyon National Park cause I imagined the cave structure of the Underworld looking like the park. I also thought it be cool if the dimension is like overlapping in the park.</li>
<li>In terms of the mass casualties by demons and cognitohazards, I do understand where you’re coming from with too many ways of dying. But I feel like having only demons in the caves would narrow the way the MTF can be picked off. These deaths were meant to be an action-packed way of how the MTF is being picked off, sort of like the movie <em>Aliens</em> where these demons are taking them. So overall, <span style="text-decoration: underline;">the demons are the only way of killing the MTF</span>.</li>
<li>I also understood your opinion on the O5 members being involved. I wanted to have an O5 involved to cause some files to be Level 5, but like you mentioned they would have an infinite number of resources for their endeavors. So I decided to make the main character a researcher, as I felt a combination of personal notes and research actions can make an engaging story to read. So in the end, <span style="text-decoration: underline;">I changed the main character from O5-13 to a research head</span>.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
I feel like this concept as of now is as good as it can get without it being too confusing. So I hope you enjoy this new version.
