<p>Okay, I'm digging a lot of the changes you've applied here. I do, however, have a few questions for my own edification.</p>
<p>First of all, why does the MTF die? Canon is, of course, fully malleable, but I believe it would take quite an offensive force to kill off a team of well-armed individuals specifically trained in anomalous exploration like this. What does their deaths contribute to the story as a whole?</p>
<p>Now, this may be a silly question, but bear with me. Why are the demons doing this? I know it can be easy to use entities like that as antagonistic props, but even the most rudimentary of motives would help flesh them out.</p>
<p>Outside of that, my main concern here is the presence what I usually term as &quot;exploration log bloat&quot;: an exploration log that's mostly idle chatter between its participants with actual plot points few and far between. That's a problem for the draft crit stage, though.</p>
<p>Overall, I think these are questions and concerns that can be smoothed out in the process. The actual core concept has a real human struggle and a classical twist that's been adapted well to the setting. With that in mind, I'm giving this a <strong><span style="color: green">greenlight</span></strong>. Good luck!</p>

							</div>

								
					
